HST Office: the collapse ladder's group content key is unsigned.

GroupContentKey hashes the visibility of every toolbox and item of a group (nKey * 31 + bit). In a
signed 32-bit integer an ordinary group overflows after a few items, which is undefined behaviour; the
hash wraps around by design, so it is sal_uInt32, and so is the key of the width cache.

- vcl/inc/HstRibbonLadder.hxx, vcl/source/control/HstRibbonLadder.cxx, vcl/inc/PriorityMergedHBox.hxx,
  vcl/source/control/PriorityMergedHBox.cxx.

--- a/vcl/inc/HstRibbonLadder.hxx
+++ b/vcl/inc/HstRibbonLadder.hxx
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
 void SetGroupState(vcl::Window& rGroup, int nState);
 
 /** Changes when the group's content changes (contextual items shown or hidden), for width caches. */
-sal_Int32 GroupContentKey(vcl::Window& rGroup);
+sal_uInt32 GroupContentKey(vcl::Window& rGroup);
 }
 
 /* vim:set shiftwidth=4 softtabstop=4 expandtab: */
